# Docker build context exclusions.
#
# Without this file `docker build .` ships the entire working tree — measured
# at 121 GB, of which crates/ alone is 71 GB of Rust target artifacts and .git
# is 8.8 GB. Every image build (including the production one) paid that cost in
# context transfer before compiling a single line.
#
# The Go build needs only go.mod/go.sum and the packages reachable from
# ./cmd/aethelredd. Tracked Go sources live exclusively in:
#   x/ app/ third_party/ sdk/ internal/ crypto/ cmd/ network/ services/ tools/
# Everything excluded below contains no tracked .go files.

# --- Version control -------------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.github

# --- Non-Go subprojects (no tracked .go files) -----------------------------
crates/
dApps/
wallet/
frontend/
contracts/
integrations/
docs/
use cases/
tmp/

# --- Build artifacts and dependency trees ----------------------------------
**/node_modules
**/target
**/dist
**/build
**/.next
**/out
**/coverage
**/__pycache__
**/.venv
**/venv
**/.pytest_cache
**/.turbo
**/artifacts
**/cache

# --- Agent, editor and OS noise --------------------------------------------
.claude
.vscode
.idea
**/.DS_Store

# --- Local scratch state (hidden, and very large) --------------------------
# .worktrees alone measured 27 GB (git worktrees carrying .next build caches);
# .cache another 2.3 GB. Neither is part of any build.
.worktrees
.cache
.remember
.pytest_cache
.playwright-mcp
.pnpm-store

# --- Local state that must never enter an image ----------------------------
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/*.log
**/keyring-test
**/priv_validator_key.json
**/node_key.json
